{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T17:41:32.141Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "ADR 0019 specifies the effect key as a hash of (ticket, stage, effect-id, head); effects.clj hashes (ticket, stage, sink identity) with no head. The implementation is right - including head would refire on every subsequent event - so the ADR needs correcting. Separately the dedup ledger is a local append-only file, so under the horizontal scaling ADR 0021 calls preferred, N replicas send N copies of every notification. ADR 0021's narrow per-pipeline lease carve-out anticipates this and nothing implements it, while ADR 0019 reads as though structural dedup already solves it. Minor: the key uses pr-str where canonical/emit exists."} :event/parents #{"sha256-66f776fa7bc6f8bd5f1d402b5129caf43d26045c87e502e4d86c3710f527be6f"} :event/ticket #uuid "e46d6283-a822-446d-a809-41f20bcbfbec" :event/type :fact/assert}